1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,713
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:13,680
<i>I heard your son Diego</i>
<i>tried to stop the project.</i>

3
00:00:13,763 --> 00:00:16,641
<i>I'm sorry to say,</i>
<i>but if you can't control your son,</i>

4
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,226
<i>how can you control</i>
<i>the people of Ardiente?</i>

5
00:00:18,309 --> 00:00:21,020
<i>I can't help but think</i>
<i>that if Grandpa were here,</i>

6
00:00:21,104 --> 00:00:22,105
<i>we wouldn't be having these problems.</i>

7
00:00:22,188 --> 00:00:23,189
[Emilia] <i>I'm the one here.</i>

8
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:26,359
<i>And I'm more than capable</i>
<i>of solving these problems.</i>

9
00:00:26,443 --> 00:00:27,777
<i>-Wait!</i>
<i>-Miss Aguas! Miss Aguas!</i>

10
00:00:27,861 --> 00:00:29,738
[woman] <i>Mr. Mayor, make them stop!</i>

11
00:00:29,821 --> 00:00:31,406
<i>There's an innocent child here!</i>

12
00:00:31,489 --> 00:00:32,824
[clamoring]

13
00:00:32,907 --> 00:00:35,076
[Arnaldo] <i>Why can't you all understand?</i>

14
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:36,369
<i>This is for everyone!</i>

15
00:00:36,453 --> 00:00:37,787
<i>-For the town!</i>
-[Diego] <i>Lies!</i>

16
00:00:37,871 --> 00:00:40,457
[Diego] <i>It hasn't been 30 days</i>
<i>since you gave us the notice!</i>

17
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:42,834
<i>You don't have a court order</i>
<i>because we all know</i>

18
00:00:42,917 --> 00:00:44,627
<i>this didn't go through due process.</i>

19
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:45,962
<i>The farmers will file an appeal!</i>

20
00:00:46,045 --> 00:00:47,464
[Ivy] <i>Emilia, is this</i>
<i>what you really want?</i>

21
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:49,716
[Emilia] <i>We're Ardientes.</i>
<i>We get what we want.</i>

22
00:00:49,799 --> 00:00:52,218
[Ivy] <i>Jepoy, I can't leave.</i>
<i>I'm with Emilia.</i>

23
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:54,345
<i>I know she's getting suspicious of me.</i>

24
00:00:54,429 --> 00:00:55,764
[Emilia] <i>Ivy?</i>

25
00:00:55,847 --> 00:00:57,432
<i>Who were you talking to?</i>

26
00:00:57,515 --> 00:00:58,850
<i>Are you following me, Emilia?</i>

27
00:00:58,933 --> 00:01:01,019
[Diego] <i>You have no right to hurt them!</i>

28
00:01:01,102 --> 00:01:02,312
<i>I know you're just following orders,</i>

29
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:04,981
<i>but that's no reason</i>
<i>to act like criminals!</i>

30
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:08,485
<i>What we need</i>
<i>is the ownership of that land!</i>

31
00:01:08,568 --> 00:01:10,320
<i>If you don't hand it back,</i>

32
00:01:10,403 --> 00:01:12,989
<i>I will bring this issue</i>
<i>to your political enemies myself!</i>

33
00:01:13,073 --> 00:01:15,825
<i>That way, no Ardiente will win</i>
<i>in the next election!</i>

34
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:17,077
[townsfolk] <i>That's right!</i>

35
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:18,453
-[man] <i>Nimfa, are you okay?</i>
-[Loring] <i>Nimfa?</i>

36
00:01:18,536 --> 00:01:19,829
<i>Mr. Ramon got into an accident.</i>

37
00:01:19,913 --> 00:01:22,457
[goon] <i>We're screwed, Governor.</i>
<i>Mr. Fernan's daughter saw me.</i>

38
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:23,541
[Emilia] <i>What?</i>

39
00:01:23,625 --> 00:01:24,459
<i>But it's good that happened.</i>

40
00:01:24,542 --> 00:01:28,254
<i>They'll realize they shouldn't be</i>
<i>going against the Ardientes.</i>

41
00:01:35,136 --> 00:01:36,513
Have you heard the news?

42
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:37,847
Someone from the co-op died.

43
00:01:37,931 --> 00:01:39,265
Yes, it was Mr. Ramon.

44
00:01:39,349 --> 00:01:41,226
Mr. Fernan's right-hand man,
leader of the co-op.

45
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:44,979
Another one bites the dust.

46
00:01:45,063 --> 00:01:46,564
Life is really fleeting.

47
00:01:46,648 --> 00:01:48,566
That's why

48
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:52,320
you have to celebrate your successes,
your little victories.

49
00:01:52,821 --> 00:01:56,282
Otherwise, life is just
going to pass you by.

50
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:58,201
How sad.

51
00:01:58,284 --> 00:01:59,702
Is that all you can say, Emilia?

52
00:02:01,621 --> 00:02:06,084
Just the other day, Ramon
went here to plead with you.

53
00:02:06,167 --> 00:02:07,252
[tense music]

54
00:02:07,335 --> 00:02:10,380
Raul, are you insinuating I have
something to do with his death?

55
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:13,007
Not really.

56
00:02:14,259 --> 00:02:17,220
But with all the people you had killed,

57
00:02:17,303 --> 00:02:19,264
you might as well be the Grim Reaper.

58
00:02:19,347 --> 00:02:21,266
Or maybe you're his proxy.

59
00:02:22,225 --> 00:02:23,601
Just think about it.

60
00:02:23,685 --> 00:02:26,229
You had your own son beaten up.

61
00:02:26,312 --> 00:02:27,480
And what about Orallo?

62
00:02:27,564 --> 00:02:30,233
I'm sure you had something
to do with his death

63
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:34,154
to cover up your gambling operations.

64
00:02:34,237 --> 00:02:36,281
And now, you had a farmer killed?

65
00:02:37,448 --> 00:02:43,163
I only did what I had to do
to save our family.

66
00:02:43,246 --> 00:02:46,082
Because if I didn't, we would've
all gone down in flames!

67
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:47,292
[utensils clatter]

68
00:02:51,754 --> 00:02:53,089
You always make decisions

69
00:02:53,172 --> 00:02:55,049
without thinking of the consequences.

70
00:02:55,133 --> 00:02:58,219
It's no wonder Grandpa
still can't trust you.

71
00:02:58,303 --> 00:03:00,471
[tense music intensifies]

72
00:03:00,555 --> 00:03:02,015
[Emilia] What's your point?

73
00:03:02,098 --> 00:03:03,516
You think you're better than me

74
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:05,560
just because your grandfather
trusts you more?

75
00:03:06,561 --> 00:03:08,354
You don't know how hard it is

76
00:03:08,438 --> 00:03:09,731
to take his place.

77
00:03:09,814 --> 00:03:13,484
I bear the pain
of making decisions for this family!

78
00:03:14,485 --> 00:03:17,322
So don't you tell me that you know better

79
00:03:17,405 --> 00:03:20,283
because, frankly, you won't
be able to handle it.

80
00:03:21,409 --> 00:03:24,412
[unsettling music playing]

81
00:03:38,384 --> 00:03:41,012
[sighs]

82
00:03:41,095 --> 00:03:43,473
[squeals in frustration, heavy breathing]

83
00:03:51,981 --> 00:03:54,067
[groans in frustration, heavy breathing]

84
00:04:00,657 --> 00:04:02,033
[line ringing]

85
00:04:02,116 --> 00:04:04,702
Vic, how's Grandpa? Is he conscious yet?

86
00:04:04,786 --> 00:04:06,371
Not yet, Mayor.

87
00:04:08,539 --> 00:04:09,958
Where's his doctor? I want to talk to him.

88
00:04:10,541 --> 00:04:12,335
[Vic] <i>All right, sir. Hold on.</i>

89
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:15,672
Doc, Mayor Ardiente-Torillo
is on the line.

90
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:18,299
[York] <i>Hello?</i>

91
00:04:18,383 --> 00:04:20,301
Doc, this is Mayor Ardiente-Torillo.

92
00:04:20,385 --> 00:04:21,344
How's the congressman?

93
00:04:21,427 --> 00:04:23,680
After his triple bypass operation,

94
00:04:23,763 --> 00:04:27,100
we're closely monitoring
his body's reaction to the surgery.

95
00:04:27,725 --> 00:04:30,603
When will he be discharged?
When can he come back?

96
00:04:30,687 --> 00:04:33,690
It will take quite some time
for him to heal completely.

97
00:04:33,773 --> 00:04:35,733
<i>After which, we'll enroll him</i>

98
00:04:35,817 --> 00:04:38,194
in a comprehensive
cardiac rehabilitation program.

99
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:40,405
So, he will need some time.

100
00:04:42,949 --> 00:04:44,200
Can I talk to him?

101
00:04:44,867 --> 00:04:46,703
I'm sorry. He's still asleep.

102
00:04:47,578 --> 00:04:50,123
But don't worry, we're taking
good care of him.

103
00:04:51,207 --> 00:04:52,834
Okay, thank you.

104
00:04:53,459 --> 00:04:57,922
[unsettling music playing]

105
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:03,219
[Diego] Mom!

106
00:05:04,554 --> 00:05:05,722
Mom!

107
00:05:06,347 --> 00:05:08,808
-Mom!
-And what's with that noise?

108
00:05:08,891 --> 00:05:10,226
Mom!

109
00:05:10,810 --> 00:05:12,395
Oh, you're here.

110
00:05:12,478 --> 00:05:14,605
You didn't even bother to check on us.

111
00:05:14,689 --> 00:05:17,191
-Should I still worry about you?
-That's not why I'm here!

112
00:05:18,359 --> 00:05:19,819
And then, what?

113
00:05:20,403 --> 00:05:21,696
Did you have Mr. Ramon killed?

114
00:05:21,779 --> 00:05:23,698
[tense music intensifies]

115
00:05:23,781 --> 00:05:25,283
Did you have him killed?

116
00:05:25,366 --> 00:05:26,951
-What?
-Mr. Ramon.

117
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:30,872
The man who threatened to side
with our political enemies.

118
00:05:30,955 --> 00:05:32,457
Did you have him killed?

119
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:35,043
Why are those farmers' future
more important to you

120
00:05:35,126 --> 00:05:37,086
than the future of this town?

121
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:39,630
Mom, you don't have the right to decide

122
00:05:40,423 --> 00:05:42,258
whether someone's life
is important or not.

123
00:05:43,342 --> 00:05:45,344
You're just a governor, not a god!

124
00:05:45,428 --> 00:05:46,554
[Arnaldo] Diego, that's enough.

125
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:51,059
Did you know about this?

126
00:05:51,142 --> 00:05:52,226
It doesn't matter.

127
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:54,604
People die every day.

128
00:05:54,687 --> 00:05:56,105
That's how life is.

129
00:05:56,564 --> 00:05:57,690
You just have to deal with it.

130
00:06:01,152 --> 00:06:02,779
[exhales]

131
00:06:03,279 --> 00:06:05,073
You always tell me…

132
00:06:06,991 --> 00:06:08,826
that I don't act like an Ardiente.

133
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:11,662
[melodramatic music playing]

134
00:06:13,039 --> 00:06:14,624
[sniffles] I wish it was true.

135
00:06:14,707 --> 00:06:18,127
I wish I wasn't born an Ardiente!

136
00:06:18,211 --> 00:06:21,923
[melodramatic music playing]

137
00:06:25,301 --> 00:06:28,221
I wish you weren't born
an Ardiente either.

138
00:06:28,888 --> 00:06:31,057
If you're sick and tired of this family,

139
00:06:31,140 --> 00:06:34,268
then, by all means, leave!
Do you understand?

140
00:06:35,853 --> 00:06:40,024
I swear I won't come back here

141
00:06:40,108 --> 00:06:44,403
until I prove you had a hand
in Mr. Ramon's death

142
00:06:44,487 --> 00:06:46,823
and the other killings in this town!

143
00:06:53,955 --> 00:06:56,958
[somber music playing]

144
00:07:11,556 --> 00:07:12,682
[gun cocking]

145
00:07:14,434 --> 00:07:15,351
[Emilia] You know, Ivy?

146
00:07:15,435 --> 00:07:17,687
After all the stress
that I've gone through,

147
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:19,397
this is what I need.

148
00:07:20,523 --> 00:07:22,233
[gunshot rings out]

149
00:07:22,316 --> 00:07:25,695
[unsettling music playing]

150
00:07:30,116 --> 00:07:31,200
[gun cocking]

151
00:07:34,704 --> 00:07:35,746
[gunshot rings out]

152
00:07:45,173 --> 00:07:47,508
Good job, there! Almost bull's-eye.

153
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:51,762
Yeah, almost. But it's not enough.

154
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:55,057
You should hit the heart, at the center,

155
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:59,604
where your enemies'
greatest desires and fears lie.

156
00:08:00,354 --> 00:08:01,981
That's where you should aim at.

157
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:07,612
Well, Ivy, speaking
of enemies, take a look at this.

158
00:08:08,905 --> 00:08:09,947
Look.

159
00:08:10,656 --> 00:08:12,116
Read this article.

160
00:08:12,909 --> 00:08:17,830
It seems like you're taking
Diego and the co-op's side.

161
00:08:18,706 --> 00:08:20,333
Aren't they our enemies?

162
00:08:23,503 --> 00:08:25,880
It's strange, Ivy, isn't it?

163
00:08:25,963 --> 00:08:27,423
The very person

164
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:29,675
who will benefit from this project

165
00:08:29,759 --> 00:08:31,427
is the same person delaying it.

166
00:08:32,678 --> 00:08:34,764
You know, I just find it so weird.

167
00:08:35,389 --> 00:08:37,266
Can you please enlighten me?

168
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:40,978
[tense music playing]

169
00:08:44,398 --> 00:08:46,150
[chuckling]

170
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:48,611
Did you fall for that too, Emilia?

171
00:08:50,404 --> 00:08:52,073
I must be a really good actress.

172
00:08:53,991 --> 00:08:55,243
Emilia.

173
00:08:55,993 --> 00:08:57,370
I'm a strategist.

174
00:08:57,995 --> 00:09:00,540
First, I agreed to hold a dialogue.

175
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:04,043
Second, at the dispersal,

176
00:09:04,126 --> 00:09:08,631
I showed everyone
how much I care for them.

177
00:09:10,049 --> 00:09:15,346
Now, I know that they trust me.

178
00:09:16,138 --> 00:09:22,979
I also know that they see me
as a true friend.

179
00:09:23,813 --> 00:09:26,065
And before they know it…

180
00:09:26,649 --> 00:09:27,733
Boom!

181
00:09:28,818 --> 00:09:30,695
I already got what I want.

182
00:09:33,155 --> 00:09:34,407
Really?

183
00:09:35,658 --> 00:09:37,285
As for me…

184
00:09:38,286 --> 00:09:40,079
I have two styles.

185
00:09:41,330 --> 00:09:43,708
The first is the long route.

186
00:09:43,791 --> 00:09:49,046
It's for the farmers
who I can get rid of like ants.

187
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:50,006
[gunshot rings out]

188
00:09:53,009 --> 00:09:54,510
What's the second route?

189
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,140
Same as yours, Ivy.

190
00:10:00,766 --> 00:10:02,351
But only deadlier.

191
00:10:06,606 --> 00:10:09,984
That's why we're really
good friends, Emilia.

192
00:10:14,488 --> 00:10:15,615
[gunshot rings out]

193
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,243
[gasps]

194
00:10:19,327 --> 00:10:20,369
Bull's-eye?

195
00:10:30,921 --> 00:10:32,757
So, I have to leave.

196
00:10:33,841 --> 00:10:35,718
I still need to take care
of some business matters.

197
00:10:36,427 --> 00:10:38,304
Okay, Ivy, thank you.

198
00:10:40,222 --> 00:10:43,726
I'm happy that we're still
friends and allies.

199
00:10:45,102 --> 00:10:46,395
Of course.

200
00:10:46,479 --> 00:10:48,397
We're still allies, Emilia.

201
00:10:52,026 --> 00:10:54,111
[phone ringing]

202
00:10:55,404 --> 00:10:56,447
Hello?

203
00:10:57,490 --> 00:10:58,699
Good.

204
00:10:59,408 --> 00:11:03,162
Just make sure you took care
of things smoothly.

205
00:11:04,163 --> 00:11:05,206
Good job.

206
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:08,918
Ivy.

207
00:11:09,001 --> 00:11:10,961
-Are you okay?
-My staff called.

208
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:13,005
One of my constituents just died.

209
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:15,091
It's so unfortunate, Ivy.

210
00:11:15,174 --> 00:11:16,467
It was Mr. Ramon from the co-op.

211
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:19,595
[sighs] I forgot his last name.

212
00:11:20,513 --> 00:11:21,931
You know what?

213
00:11:22,014 --> 00:11:24,975
I have a feeling this happened
because he crossed someone.

214
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:29,730
I mean, it's so easy
to offend people these days.

215
00:11:29,814 --> 00:11:31,941
You should always be careful.

216
00:11:32,775 --> 00:11:36,404
Or else, you'll be one cold statistic.

217
00:11:39,323 --> 00:11:42,660
Oh, um, Ivy, can you do me
a favor, please?

218
00:11:42,743 --> 00:11:46,247
Can you send my condolences
to Mr. Ramon's family?

219
00:11:49,458 --> 00:11:52,294
Can you also go to the wake on my behalf?

220
00:11:52,378 --> 00:11:54,130
After all, you're my consultant.

221
00:11:54,922 --> 00:11:57,591
[unsettling music playing]

222
00:12:04,723 --> 00:12:06,183
I'll do it, Emilia.

223
00:12:08,727 --> 00:12:10,438
But can I ask a favor too?

224
00:12:11,897 --> 00:12:16,068
I hope we can put off the EPZ for now.

225
00:12:17,862 --> 00:12:19,905
They just lost a member.

226
00:12:21,073 --> 00:12:22,575
Things may just get worse.

227
00:12:26,454 --> 00:12:30,291
Sure! We really should
put the project on hold for now.

228
00:12:30,916 --> 00:12:31,959
Yeah.

229
00:12:33,419 --> 00:12:34,545
I have to go.

230
00:12:34,628 --> 00:12:36,464
All right. Bye, Ivy.

231
00:12:42,303 --> 00:12:45,723
Are you really going to
the co-op like Emilia asked?

232
00:12:47,933 --> 00:12:49,977
Why would I obey Emilia?

233
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:51,645
I just want to go to the co-op.

234
00:12:52,188 --> 00:12:54,690
She wants you to take
the brunt of their anger.

235
00:12:54,773 --> 00:12:56,442
It was one of their members, remember?

236
00:12:57,193 --> 00:12:59,862
Ivy, it's too dangerous.

237
00:12:59,945 --> 00:13:01,447
I don't want anything bad
to happen to you.

238
00:13:01,530 --> 00:13:02,990
I can handle it, Jepoy.

239
00:13:03,073 --> 00:13:04,492
I'm coming with you.

240
00:13:04,575 --> 00:13:05,868
Jepoy!

241
00:13:06,619 --> 00:13:08,245
Can you please stop?

242
00:13:09,288 --> 00:13:15,127
Your job is to support my plans,
not to mess with my decisions.

243
00:13:20,174 --> 00:13:21,008
[sighs]

244
00:13:21,926 --> 00:13:23,135
Sorry.

245
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:26,096
Please try to understand.

246
00:13:27,515 --> 00:13:32,186
Jepoy, I'm going to the co-op
not because Emilia asked me to.

247
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:34,980
I'm going there to pay my respects

248
00:13:35,064 --> 00:13:38,400
because we both know
what Emilia did was wrong.

249
00:13:38,484 --> 00:13:39,443
You know me.

250
00:13:40,027 --> 00:13:41,820
I don't want to see anyone
being oppressed,

251
00:13:41,904 --> 00:13:43,948
especially in the hands of the Ardientes.

252
00:13:44,907 --> 00:13:46,408
I'm sorry too.

253
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:47,743
I was just worried about your safety.

254
00:13:49,245 --> 00:13:50,287
I know.

255
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:52,498
What if Emilia doubts you?

256
00:13:53,207 --> 00:13:55,876
Like I said, I know what I'm doing.

257
00:13:58,003 --> 00:14:00,172
All right. I'll keep you posted.

258
00:14:05,302 --> 00:14:07,888
NEW ARDIENTE

259
00:14:10,099 --> 00:14:12,393
[Ivy] <i>We've succeeded for now.</i>

260
00:14:12,476 --> 00:14:15,563
<i>The Ardientes won't</i>
<i>take your land just yet.</i>

261
00:14:18,691 --> 00:14:24,238
<i>I promise I will never forget</i>
<i>what happened to that farmer.</i>

262
00:14:29,076 --> 00:14:32,621
<i>It's one of the crimes</i>
<i>the Ardientes will pay for.</i>

263
00:14:33,455 --> 00:14:36,250
<i>I will get justice for his death.</i>

264
00:14:38,043 --> 00:14:40,462
<i>And for my parents' deaths too.</i>

265
00:14:46,677 --> 00:14:47,845
[Nimfa] Have some biscuits.

266
00:14:47,928 --> 00:14:50,639
If the Governor indeed had Ramon killed,

267
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:53,893
I think they want to send us a message.

268
00:14:53,976 --> 00:14:57,605
They want us to stop going against them.

269
00:14:58,355 --> 00:15:02,276
But what they're doing isn't right.

270
00:15:03,319 --> 00:15:05,237
This is all your fault.

271
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:07,114
-What?
-Us?

272
00:15:07,865 --> 00:15:09,617
This is Diego's fault.

273
00:15:10,409 --> 00:15:12,578
You think you know everything.

274
00:15:13,454 --> 00:15:16,415
In the first place,
we shouldn't have fought back.

275
00:15:16,498 --> 00:15:19,251
We can't win against them, anyway.

276
00:15:20,586 --> 00:15:25,215
Diego was just giving us false hope.

277
00:15:25,299 --> 00:15:27,217
-Dolfo.
-That's not true.

278
00:15:27,301 --> 00:15:28,385
Come on.

279
00:15:29,845 --> 00:15:31,555
[phone ringing]

280
00:15:33,390 --> 00:15:35,225
[car door clicks shut]

281
00:15:37,436 --> 00:15:38,896
Hello, Joan?

282
00:15:39,813 --> 00:15:40,898
Yes, okay.

283
00:15:42,024 --> 00:15:43,943
Okay, sure. No problem.

284
00:15:44,026 --> 00:15:45,986
All right, thanks.

285
00:15:47,655 --> 00:15:50,240
[engine revving]

286
00:16:01,377 --> 00:16:05,047
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

287
00:16:42,793 --> 00:16:44,294
Yes, madam?

288
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:48,173
Lara, would you know if Ivy
went to visit the co-op today?

289
00:16:49,758 --> 00:16:51,093
Uh…

290
00:16:51,176 --> 00:16:52,219
Yes, madam.

291
00:16:52,302 --> 00:16:56,181
Miss Aguas scheduled a visit
to the co-op as your consultant.

292
00:16:56,724 --> 00:16:57,808
Good.

293
00:17:02,479 --> 00:17:04,940
-Miss Carlotta.
-Yes, Jepoy?

294
00:17:05,024 --> 00:17:06,150
Is Ivy home yet?

295
00:17:06,233 --> 00:17:07,609
Oh, I don't know.

296
00:17:07,693 --> 00:17:10,571
She just said she's going to
drop by the co-op.

297
00:17:10,654 --> 00:17:12,156
-The co-op?
-Yes.

298
00:17:13,073 --> 00:17:14,450
She still went there.

299
00:17:16,201 --> 00:17:18,412
-Okay, excuse me.
-Jepoy, wait.

300
00:17:18,495 --> 00:17:20,873
Please don't worry about her too much.

301
00:17:20,956 --> 00:17:23,083
Ivy can take care of herself.

302
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:27,421
We're here to love and support her.

303
00:17:28,005 --> 00:17:30,090
That's our role in her life.

304
00:17:30,174 --> 00:17:34,219
So, let's do it the best way we can.

305
00:17:35,637 --> 00:17:36,805
Even if it hurts.

306
00:17:36,889 --> 00:17:38,807
[phone ringing]

307
00:17:45,147 --> 00:17:46,315
Hello, Mayor?

308
00:17:46,398 --> 00:17:48,192
[Arnaldo] <i>Report to me at my office.</i>

309
00:17:48,275 --> 00:17:49,693
<i>Be there in 30 minutes.</i>

310
00:17:50,402 --> 00:17:51,737
Yes, sir.

311
00:17:52,404 --> 00:17:53,822
[sighs]

312
00:17:56,909 --> 00:17:58,035
I have to go.

313
00:17:58,118 --> 00:17:59,661
All right. Take care.

314
00:18:01,288 --> 00:18:04,833
Madam, won't you be going
with Miss Aguas to the co-op?

315
00:18:07,795 --> 00:18:08,837
No.

316
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:12,174
Because that's her job as my consultant.

317
00:18:13,008 --> 00:18:15,219
To tell you the truth,
I don't find her good at all.

318
00:18:15,302 --> 00:18:16,970
She's been a failure lately.

319
00:18:17,721 --> 00:18:19,932
Lucky for her, she's my friend.

320
00:18:20,015 --> 00:18:23,060
I can see that you trust her
as your friend.

321
00:18:23,143 --> 00:18:26,647
Well, let's just say
there is a close friend,

322
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:30,025
a best friend, or a casual friend.

323
00:18:30,109 --> 00:18:32,111
And then, there's a frenemy.

324
00:18:33,821 --> 00:18:35,656
But in times of crisis…

325
00:18:38,242 --> 00:18:39,409
I'll save myself first.

326
00:18:45,833 --> 00:18:48,502
Stop pointing fingers, Dolfo.

327
00:18:48,585 --> 00:18:51,171
Diego did a lot of things for the co-op.

328
00:18:51,255 --> 00:18:52,339
That's right.

329
00:18:52,422 --> 00:18:54,633
If it weren't for him,
you wouldn't have a job.

330
00:18:56,176 --> 00:19:00,097
If not Diego, then you're
the ones to be blamed.

331
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:03,851
-What?
-What have we done, Dolfo?

332
00:19:03,934 --> 00:19:09,314
It's because you tried to befriend

333
00:19:10,149 --> 00:19:12,818
that Miss Ivy Aguas!

334
00:19:13,986 --> 00:19:17,573
You shouldn't have trusted that rich snob.

335
00:19:19,533 --> 00:19:24,413
I bet she's the one who urged the Governor

336
00:19:25,164 --> 00:19:27,749
to have my son killed!

337
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:29,585
-We don't know that, Dolfo.
-That's enough.

338
00:19:29,668 --> 00:19:32,087
-[Dolfo] She had my son killed!
-[Loring] Hold on!

339
00:19:32,171 --> 00:19:37,050
-If I see that Ivy Aguas…
-Mr. Dolfo, that's enough.

340
00:19:37,634 --> 00:19:40,304
Mr. Dolfo, please sit down.

341
00:19:40,971 --> 00:19:42,890
-Nimfa, get a cup of coffee…
-Diego!

342
00:19:42,973 --> 00:19:45,851
-…so he'll come to his senses.
-Mr. Dolfo, you need to relax.

343
00:19:45,934 --> 00:19:48,187
[Dolfo] Where is that woman?

344
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:49,897
Calm down, Mr. Dolfo.

345
00:19:52,357 --> 00:19:53,525
Where have you been?

346
00:19:53,609 --> 00:19:56,028
I've been waiting for you.
We're supposed to visit Natalie.

347
00:19:57,905 --> 00:19:59,072
Madrigal.

348
00:19:59,656 --> 00:20:01,408
What's wrong? You look distracted.

349
00:20:03,118 --> 00:20:06,705
Mayor, I heard Miss Aguas
was going to visit the co-op.

350
00:20:08,415 --> 00:20:09,833
Why would she go there?

351
00:20:09,917 --> 00:20:12,169
She knows the farmers
have a rift with the Ardientes.

352
00:20:14,129 --> 00:20:15,088
Natalie can wait.

353
00:20:15,172 --> 00:20:16,840
Get the car. We're going to see Ivy.

354
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:18,008
Yes, Mayor.

355
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:22,804
[unsettling music playing]

356
00:20:24,348 --> 00:20:25,349
Nimfa?

357
00:20:27,059 --> 00:20:28,393
What are you doing here?

358
00:20:29,019 --> 00:20:30,520
Nimfa, I'm here to pay my respects.

359
00:20:30,604 --> 00:20:31,563
[Nimfa scoffs]

360
00:20:31,647 --> 00:20:32,648
What for?

361
00:20:33,565 --> 00:20:35,275
So you can play us for fools again?

362
00:20:35,359 --> 00:20:39,321
-Nimfa, no--
-Oh, come on, Ma'am Ivy.

363
00:20:40,447 --> 00:20:42,783
You came here with the Mayor last time.

364
00:20:42,866 --> 00:20:45,661
You even helped us during the dispersal.

365
00:20:46,912 --> 00:20:48,205
[scoffs]

366
00:20:48,288 --> 00:20:49,665
But the truth is…

367
00:20:50,457 --> 00:20:52,960
you're the one provoking
the Governor and the Mayor.

368
00:20:54,503 --> 00:20:56,088
You know, Nimfa…

369
00:20:56,171 --> 00:20:58,507
You can drop the act now.

370
00:20:59,883 --> 00:21:01,677
You're just ruining our lives.

371
00:21:02,344 --> 00:21:04,304
Nimfa, wait. Listen to me first.

372
00:21:04,888 --> 00:21:08,308
I'm here to extend my sympathies.

373
00:21:09,309 --> 00:21:13,230
I also want to tell everyone
that the project is on hold.

374
00:21:13,313 --> 00:21:14,439
That's why I'm here.

375
00:21:14,523 --> 00:21:15,607
[scoffs]

376
00:21:16,608 --> 00:21:18,110
Wow!

377
00:21:18,193 --> 00:21:19,945
Well, thank you for that.

378
00:21:20,904 --> 00:21:22,197
You know what?

379
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:24,950
Ever since you came here,

380
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:26,451
there's been nothing but trouble for us.

381
00:21:26,535 --> 00:21:28,328
-Nimfa.
-You know what you are?

382
00:21:28,412 --> 00:21:29,913
You're a pest!

383
00:21:31,456 --> 00:21:32,833
You're a pest!

384
00:21:32,916 --> 00:21:33,709
[squeals in pain]

385
00:21:33,792 --> 00:21:35,252
Diego needs to know about this.

386
00:21:35,335 --> 00:21:37,713
[Nimfa grunts]

387
00:21:37,796 --> 00:21:39,089
Nimfa?

388
00:21:39,172 --> 00:21:41,091
Are you okay? Come on.

389
00:21:42,843 --> 00:21:44,803
-Let me help you.
-I don't need your help.

390
00:21:44,886 --> 00:21:46,138
Nimfa.

391
00:21:46,763 --> 00:21:48,348
I said I don't need your help!

392
00:21:50,017 --> 00:21:51,435
-That's enough.
-My son…

393
00:21:51,518 --> 00:21:52,769
Diego! Mr. Fernan!

394
00:21:52,853 --> 00:21:55,188
-Nimfa's fighting with someone.
-What?

395
00:21:55,272 --> 00:21:56,982
-[Fernan] Nimfa!
-Let's go.

396
00:21:57,065 --> 00:21:58,859
Mario, look after Mr. Dolfo.

397
00:21:58,942 --> 00:22:01,028
-Dolfo.
-[Diego] Nimfa!

398
00:22:01,111 --> 00:22:02,738
Nimfa, I'm not your enemy.

399
00:22:03,655 --> 00:22:05,365
Nimfa, I'm on your side.

400
00:22:05,449 --> 00:22:07,492
Let me help you. Come on.

401
00:22:07,576 --> 00:22:08,702
What's going on here?

402
00:22:09,661 --> 00:22:10,746
Ivy?

403
00:22:11,413 --> 00:22:12,748
Nimfa, what happened?

404
00:22:12,831 --> 00:22:13,957
Uh…

405
00:22:15,250 --> 00:22:18,128
Nimfa fell over, so I helped her up.

406
00:22:19,629 --> 00:22:20,839
Uh…

407
00:22:24,426 --> 00:22:27,137
I'm really sorry. I just came here because

408
00:22:27,679 --> 00:22:31,016
I want to offer my condolences

409
00:22:31,516 --> 00:22:34,227
and to tell you that
the project is on hold.

410
00:22:35,270 --> 00:22:37,939
Who made that decision?
Will it really happen this time?

411
00:22:38,023 --> 00:22:40,275
We've heard that many times before.

412
00:22:40,358 --> 00:22:43,612
After the dialogue, you told us
you'd look into our case.

413
00:22:44,529 --> 00:22:46,073
But what did you do?

414
00:22:46,156 --> 00:22:47,449
You ordered our dispersal.

415
00:22:48,617 --> 00:22:50,410
-Mr. Fernan.
-[Loring] And now,

416
00:22:50,494 --> 00:22:55,665
one of us died after protesting
against your project.

417
00:22:55,749 --> 00:22:58,085
And now, you're telling us
the project's on hold?

418
00:22:58,168 --> 00:23:00,796
Did someone have to die first
before you realized

419
00:23:00,879 --> 00:23:02,380
what you're doing is wrong?

420
00:23:02,464 --> 00:23:05,550
You know what?
Maybe it's best that you leave.

421
00:23:07,052 --> 00:23:10,055
[unsettling music playing]

422
00:23:15,393 --> 00:23:16,561
Mayor.

423
00:23:16,645 --> 00:23:17,687
Madrigal.

424
00:23:17,771 --> 00:23:19,648
How did you know that Ivy
went to the cooperative?

425
00:23:23,902 --> 00:23:25,362
The Governor said so.

426
00:23:27,197 --> 00:23:28,949
I heard her talking on the phone

427
00:23:29,032 --> 00:23:30,867
and she mentioned that
Miss Aguas will go to the co-op.

428
00:23:33,245 --> 00:23:34,412
Is that so?

429
00:23:35,122 --> 00:23:36,123
Let's go.

430
00:23:36,832 --> 00:23:38,750
Mr. Fernan, Nanny, Uncle.

431
00:23:38,834 --> 00:23:40,043
-Let's hear her out--
-Diego.

432
00:23:41,545 --> 00:23:42,671
It's okay.

433
00:23:42,754 --> 00:23:44,381
I understand them.

434
00:23:44,464 --> 00:23:45,590
[Dolfo] You!

435
00:23:47,300 --> 00:23:48,927
-You monster!
-[screaming]

436
00:23:49,010 --> 00:23:50,554
Mr. Dolfo!

437
00:23:50,637 --> 00:23:53,682
[tense music playing]

438
00:23:54,683 --> 00:23:56,184
-[Diego] Mr. Dolfo!
-[Nimfa] Mr. Dolfo!

439
00:23:56,268 --> 00:23:58,436
-You're a monster!
-[Diego] Drop the machete!

440
00:23:58,520 --> 00:24:00,188
That woman is a monster!

441
00:24:00,272 --> 00:24:01,815
She's the one who put us in this mess!

442
00:24:01,898 --> 00:24:05,527
They're stealing our land!
They're ruining our livelihood!

443
00:24:05,610 --> 00:24:07,362
-[man] That's enough!
-Dolfo, stop it.

444
00:24:07,445 --> 00:24:09,406
She's nothing but a greedy businesswoman!

445
00:24:09,489 --> 00:24:11,783
-A greedy monster!
-Mr. Dolfo, that's enough!

446
00:24:11,867 --> 00:24:14,077
We understand what you feel,

447
00:24:14,161 --> 00:24:16,163
but you don't have to blame other people.

448
00:24:16,246 --> 00:24:18,165
What's done is done.

449
00:24:18,248 --> 00:24:19,791
-This isn't Ivy's fault!
-No!

450
00:24:19,875 --> 00:24:23,545
We'll do everything to get justice
for Mr. Ramon's death.

451
00:24:23,628 --> 00:24:24,963
It's her fault!

452
00:24:25,547 --> 00:24:27,215
She must pay for this with her life!

453
00:24:27,299 --> 00:24:29,426
-[man] That's enough, Dolfo.
-She needs to die!

454
00:24:29,509 --> 00:24:31,178
-Let's go.
-That's enough.

455
00:24:31,261 --> 00:24:32,971
-[man] Stop it, Dolfo.
-[Dolfo] It's her fault!

456
00:24:33,054 --> 00:24:35,098
-[man] Let's go, Dolfo.
-[Dolfo] She's a thief!

457
00:24:35,724 --> 00:24:37,642
[Dolfo screaming]

458
00:24:37,726 --> 00:24:38,727
Ivy?

459
00:24:40,896 --> 00:24:42,189
-[Ivy] I'll be going now.
-Ivy.

460
00:24:44,608 --> 00:24:45,817
You're hurt.

461
00:24:46,401 --> 00:24:47,903
-It's okay. I'll be fine.
-Ivy, wait!

462
00:24:48,695 --> 00:24:49,905
We have to treat your wound.

463
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:56,494
Nanny.

464
00:24:56,578 --> 00:24:57,704
Where's Raul?

465
00:24:57,787 --> 00:25:00,207
Ma'am, he's at the porch,
talking to a woman.

466
00:25:00,290 --> 00:25:02,417
A woman? Who?

467
00:25:04,628 --> 00:25:06,004
[Raul chuckles]

468
00:25:06,087 --> 00:25:07,547
[Raul] You look great.

469
00:25:07,631 --> 00:25:09,758
You're still as beautiful as ever.

470
00:25:09,841 --> 00:25:10,967
[Claire giggles]

471
00:25:11,051 --> 00:25:13,178
Such a smooth talker, Raul.

472
00:25:13,261 --> 00:25:15,263
I noticed you look younger.

473
00:25:15,347 --> 00:25:18,475
-Come on.
-Tell me, are you in love?

474
00:25:19,017 --> 00:25:22,520
Only with his beautiful wife and capable--

475
00:25:23,438 --> 00:25:24,648
Aunt Claire?

476
00:25:26,107 --> 00:25:28,151
Auntie, what are you doing here?

477
00:25:28,944 --> 00:25:30,111
Really, Emilia?

478
00:25:30,195 --> 00:25:32,948
After so many years
of not seeing each other,

479
00:25:33,031 --> 00:25:34,908
that's how you greet me?

480
00:25:35,617 --> 00:25:37,285
[scoffs] How about…

481
00:25:38,536 --> 00:25:40,205
"I miss you, Auntie Claire?"

482
00:25:40,789 --> 00:25:42,374
Of course, Auntie. Have a seat.

483
00:25:42,457 --> 00:25:47,879
I missed you. My favorite
aunt and my mom's youngest sister.

484
00:25:50,799 --> 00:25:53,551
I'm sorry I haven't visited in so long.

485
00:25:53,635 --> 00:25:55,720
Even after your mom passed away.

486
00:25:56,304 --> 00:25:58,890
You know how I never got along
with your boorish father.

487
00:25:58,974 --> 00:26:00,934
And now that he's not around,

488
00:26:01,017 --> 00:26:04,271
I figured now
is the best time to visit you.

489
00:26:04,813 --> 00:26:07,440
Well, you just really
surprised me, Aunt Claire.

490
00:26:08,066 --> 00:26:09,484
Why?

491
00:26:09,567 --> 00:26:12,821
Do you have a weak heart like Julio?

492
00:26:12,904 --> 00:26:15,365
Politics made you paranoid, my dear.

493
00:26:15,991 --> 00:26:17,701
No, Auntie.

494
00:26:17,784 --> 00:26:22,872
I just want to be sure that
the people who enter my house

495
00:26:22,956 --> 00:26:24,916
are my allies and not my enemies.

496
00:26:28,837 --> 00:26:30,880
Spoken like a true Ardiente.

497
00:26:30,964 --> 00:26:31,798
[chuckles]

498
00:26:31,881 --> 00:26:35,135
I'm sure my sister is so proud of you.

499
00:26:35,927 --> 00:26:38,888
After all, you're now
the one sitting on the throne.

500
00:26:39,556 --> 00:26:41,308
We should celebrate that, right?

501
00:26:41,391 --> 00:26:43,351
Yes, Auntie. I missed you!

502
00:26:43,435 --> 00:26:45,395
I missed you too.

503
00:26:45,478 --> 00:26:47,939
-Welcome back.
-It's so nice to see you.

504
00:26:53,028 --> 00:26:54,446
Wait here, Mayor.

505
00:26:54,529 --> 00:26:55,655
[car door clicks shut]

506
00:26:57,907 --> 00:26:59,075
Bro, hold on.

507
00:27:00,160 --> 00:27:01,745
What's happening?

508
00:27:01,828 --> 00:27:03,747
Mr. Dolfo got mad and grabbed a machete.

509
00:27:03,830 --> 00:27:05,707
He tried to attack Miss Ivy.

510
00:27:05,790 --> 00:27:07,083
Ivy?

511
00:27:10,295 --> 00:27:11,463
Let's go. Move.

512
00:27:13,631 --> 00:27:14,674
[Diego] Ivy, wait!

513
00:27:14,758 --> 00:27:16,843
-Let's treat your wound.
-I can take care of myself.

514
00:27:16,926 --> 00:27:18,887
You keep saying that,
but I won't believe you

515
00:27:18,970 --> 00:27:20,722
because that's not what I see.

516
00:27:24,434 --> 00:27:25,727
You don't know what you're saying

517
00:27:25,810 --> 00:27:26,728
because you don't know me.

518
00:27:27,979 --> 00:27:29,522
I just want to make sure you're okay.

519
00:27:29,606 --> 00:27:30,940
What Mister Dolfo did was wrong.

520
00:27:31,566 --> 00:27:32,776
I said I'm fine.

521
00:27:32,859 --> 00:27:34,986
And, Diego, I understand.

522
00:27:35,570 --> 00:27:37,864
I understand why they're blaming me.

523
00:27:37,947 --> 00:27:40,158
I shouldn't have come here

524
00:27:40,241 --> 00:27:42,869
because I know you all see me as an enemy

525
00:27:42,952 --> 00:27:45,955
since you know I'm an ally
of the Ardientes.

526
00:27:46,623 --> 00:27:49,334
That's why I understand why
the people here are mad at me

527
00:27:49,417 --> 00:27:51,544
and why you are too.

528
00:27:51,628 --> 00:27:55,006
Hold on. Don't generalize us.
I'm not Mr. Dolfo.

529
00:27:55,090 --> 00:27:56,800
I don't look at you the way they do.

530
00:27:58,176 --> 00:27:59,594
I stood up for you, remember?

531
00:28:00,512 --> 00:28:02,639
Did I ask you to do that?

532
00:28:04,057 --> 00:28:05,308
Do you think…

533
00:28:06,684 --> 00:28:08,186
I'd ever let you get hurt?

534
00:28:09,187 --> 00:28:11,898
["Sa'Yo" instrumental playing]

535
00:28:12,982 --> 00:28:14,025
You're concerned?

536
00:28:16,361 --> 00:28:17,695
Wait a minute.

537
00:28:17,779 --> 00:28:20,323
Mr. Torillo, you're mad at me.

538
00:28:20,407 --> 00:28:25,412
So, please, don't pretend
that you're concerned about me.

539
00:28:31,042 --> 00:28:32,961
Could you just stop doubting me?

540
00:28:33,044 --> 00:28:34,379
That's how I really feel!

541
00:28:35,588 --> 00:28:38,717
Really now? That's how you feel?

542
00:28:39,300 --> 00:28:42,887
Aren't you mad at me?

543
00:28:43,555 --> 00:28:45,724
All you've ever done was despise me!

544
00:28:45,807 --> 00:28:47,308
What was it you said?

545
00:28:47,392 --> 00:28:49,352
That ever since I arrived
at Poblacion Ardiente,

546
00:28:49,436 --> 00:28:50,854
I've brought nothing but trouble.

547
00:28:51,438 --> 00:28:53,648
That I'm greedy for money,
like your family.

548
00:28:53,732 --> 00:28:56,901
That I'm using your brother
and your mother for this project.

549
00:28:56,985 --> 00:29:01,156
So don't tell me that you're
worried or concerned about me!

550
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:03,199
What?

551
00:29:03,825 --> 00:29:06,745
Are you eating your words now?

552
00:29:12,584 --> 00:29:15,962
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

553
00:29:38,026 --> 00:29:39,110
Let's go.

554
00:29:46,868 --> 00:29:53,124
[tender music playing]

555
00:30:00,423 --> 00:30:03,092
[heavy breathing]

556
00:30:22,111 --> 00:30:24,781
[tender music playing]

557
00:30:47,303 --> 00:30:48,805
[breathes heavily]

558
00:30:48,888 --> 00:30:50,056
No, Ivy.

559
00:30:51,099 --> 00:30:52,183
Don't.

560
00:30:54,811 --> 00:30:56,145
-Driver, let's go.
-[car engine starts]

561
00:30:58,147 --> 00:30:59,607
Ivy.

562
00:30:59,691 --> 00:31:00,733
Ivy, wait!

563
00:31:01,776 --> 00:31:03,069
Ivy!

564
00:31:30,388 --> 00:31:33,099
Diego, where's Miss Ivy?

565
00:31:33,182 --> 00:31:35,852
Has she left? Was she hurt?

566
00:31:38,187 --> 00:31:40,273
Where's Mr. Dolfo?

567
00:31:40,356 --> 00:31:41,399
Back there.

568
00:31:46,362 --> 00:31:48,406
[deep breath]

569
00:31:49,240 --> 00:31:50,867
So, Diego's trying to pull
a fast one on me.

570
00:31:53,578 --> 00:31:56,915
Make sure you find the man
who tried to hurt Ivy.

571
00:31:57,624 --> 00:31:59,792
[unsettling music playing]

572
00:32:03,129 --> 00:32:05,924
-We understand how you feel,
-Mr. Dolfo.

573
00:32:06,007 --> 00:32:08,635
-but you should take it easy.
-Mr. Dolfo, why did you do that?

574
00:32:09,719 --> 00:32:11,429
I'm sorry, Diego.

575
00:32:12,305 --> 00:32:13,973
My anger got the best of me.

576
00:32:14,807 --> 00:32:17,268
I know we're all angry right now,

577
00:32:18,019 --> 00:32:22,065
but that's not an excuse
to resort to violence.

578
00:32:23,024 --> 00:32:24,317
Everyone,

579
00:32:24,901 --> 00:32:27,487
I know it's hard to start again
after what happened,

580
00:32:27,570 --> 00:32:31,324
but we have to believe that
if we work together,

581
00:32:31,407 --> 00:32:32,825
we'll be able to bounce back.

582
00:32:32,909 --> 00:32:35,036
-That's right!
-We need to stay united.

583
00:32:35,119 --> 00:32:38,790
That's right. As long as
we help each other.

584
00:32:38,873 --> 00:32:40,875
-We have to help each other.
-You're not alone, Dolfo.

585
00:32:40,959 --> 00:32:42,210
Let's help each other.

586
00:32:43,002 --> 00:32:46,464
[tense music playing]

587
00:32:49,342 --> 00:32:51,260
[man] The cops are here.

588
00:32:51,344 --> 00:32:53,429
Good evening. We're looking
for Rodolfo Makabisbis.

589
00:32:56,516 --> 00:32:57,684
That's me.

590
00:32:58,267 --> 00:32:59,560
We have a warrant for your arrest.

591
00:33:00,144 --> 00:33:02,146
You're coming with us.

592
00:33:02,230 --> 00:33:04,232
Hold on. What did he do?

593
00:33:04,315 --> 00:33:07,276
He went berserk
and threatened Miss Aguas' life.

594
00:33:08,653 --> 00:33:11,155
Wait. Maybe we can talk this out--

595
00:33:11,239 --> 00:33:12,198
It's all right, Diego.

596
00:33:12,782 --> 00:33:13,908
This is my fault.

597
00:33:13,992 --> 00:33:16,494
Miss Aguas has every right
to have me arrested.

598
00:33:16,577 --> 00:33:19,998
-[police] Take him in.
-You're coming with us.

599
00:33:20,957 --> 00:33:22,125
-Take it easy.
-Gently, Officer.

600
00:33:22,208 --> 00:33:23,292
-Let's go.
-Diego.

601
00:33:23,376 --> 00:33:24,335
-Sir.
-Dolfo.

602
00:33:24,419 --> 00:33:26,254
[indistinct chatter]

603
00:33:26,337 --> 00:33:29,632
Mr. Dolfo, don't worry.
We'll help you get out of there.

604
00:33:37,098 --> 00:33:39,308
Diego, where are you going?

605
00:33:40,476 --> 00:33:43,646
Nanny, if Ivy's the one
who had Mr. Dolfo arrested,

606
00:33:43,730 --> 00:33:45,565
she's the only one who can free him.

607
00:33:45,648 --> 00:33:48,026
I'll be right back. I won't take too long.

608
00:33:48,109 --> 00:33:49,986
Uncle, you take care of everything here.

609
00:33:50,069 --> 00:33:52,280
-Take care, Diego.
-Everyone, I'll be back.

610
00:33:55,908 --> 00:33:59,954
Ivy, you have to be
more careful next time.

611
00:34:00,038 --> 00:34:03,082
Look what happened.
It could've been worse!

612
00:34:03,166 --> 00:34:04,459
[sighs]

613
00:34:04,542 --> 00:34:06,753
Nanny, I'm fine.

614
00:34:07,837 --> 00:34:10,840
Anyway, Diego was there.
He stood up for me.

615
00:34:10,923 --> 00:34:12,383
Well, it's a good thing he did.

616
00:34:12,467 --> 00:34:15,970
Even though you don't get along,
he still came to your rescue.

617
00:34:17,138 --> 00:34:18,347
Ivy.

618
00:34:18,431 --> 00:34:22,769
Don't you think it's about time
you told Diego the truth?

619
00:34:23,644 --> 00:34:25,480
He's already going against his family.

620
00:34:26,272 --> 00:34:29,108
I believe he'll side with what's right

621
00:34:29,192 --> 00:34:31,819
and help you seek justice.

622
00:34:33,279 --> 00:34:36,949
[somber music playing]

623
00:34:38,868 --> 00:34:40,369
It's not that easy.

624
00:34:41,746 --> 00:34:43,498
It's way too complicated.

625
00:34:45,541 --> 00:34:47,168
He actually kissed me earlier.

626
00:34:47,752 --> 00:34:49,128
What?

627
00:34:49,629 --> 00:34:51,422
He kissed you? Why?

628
00:34:55,885 --> 00:34:59,639
I don't know. It's so hard to read him.

629
00:34:59,722 --> 00:35:04,310
I mean, one day he's mad at me
and then, we're friends.

630
00:35:04,393 --> 00:35:05,812
Later, he'll get mad again.

631
00:35:06,437 --> 00:35:09,023
Earlier, he said
he was concerned about me,

632
00:35:09,107 --> 00:35:10,358
that's why he wanted to help.

633
00:35:10,983 --> 00:35:14,862
Then, I got so confused,

634
00:35:14,946 --> 00:35:19,784
so I confronted him about
the harsh things he's ever told me.

635
00:35:19,867 --> 00:35:21,786
Until it… happened.

636
00:35:24,163 --> 00:35:25,748
He kissed me.

637
00:35:25,832 --> 00:35:27,166
What?

638
00:35:27,250 --> 00:35:28,668
[scoffs]

639
00:35:29,585 --> 00:35:30,795
[scoffs]

640
00:35:33,297 --> 00:35:34,507
You know, Nanny.

641
00:35:35,591 --> 00:35:37,677
Ms. Prianka taught me…

642
00:35:39,053 --> 00:35:40,972
to always prepare for the unexpected.

643
00:35:42,682 --> 00:35:43,516
[sighs]

644
00:35:43,599 --> 00:35:45,601
But not for this.

645
00:35:48,354 --> 00:35:49,480
Ivy!

646
00:35:49,564 --> 00:35:51,107
-[doorbell rings]
-Ivy!

647
00:35:51,899 --> 00:35:53,609
-[doorbell rings]
-Ivy!

648
00:35:55,903 --> 00:35:57,613
-Ivy!
-Ivy, what should I do?

649
00:35:57,697 --> 00:36:00,408
-Ivy! Ivy!
-I'll tell him you're asleep.

650
00:36:01,868 --> 00:36:03,744
-Ivy!
-Ivy, well?

651
00:36:06,455 --> 00:36:08,291
[door clicks open]

652
00:36:08,374 --> 00:36:09,625
Yes?

653
00:36:10,418 --> 00:36:11,711
What are you doing here?

654
00:36:15,882 --> 00:36:17,341
-Well?
-About what happened earlier…

655
00:36:18,634 --> 00:36:20,011
You meant the kiss?

656
00:36:22,096 --> 00:36:23,139
[sighs]

657
00:36:23,222 --> 00:36:24,515
Diego.

658
00:36:26,184 --> 00:36:27,185
It's fine.

659
00:36:28,769 --> 00:36:30,897
It's not a big deal.

660
00:36:32,273 --> 00:36:33,858
But I shouldn't have done that.

661
00:36:35,151 --> 00:36:36,777
I'm sorry. Please forgive me.

662
00:36:39,280 --> 00:36:41,115
As I said earlier,

663
00:36:41,199 --> 00:36:42,491
it was just a kiss.

664
00:36:44,118 --> 00:36:45,620
It's nothing.

665
00:36:45,703 --> 00:36:47,955
If that's why you're here,
you can leave now.

666
00:36:49,081 --> 00:36:50,458
Ivy, wait.

667
00:36:50,541 --> 00:36:52,335
I really came here for Mr. Dolfo.

668
00:36:53,085 --> 00:36:54,837
I know what he did was wrong,

669
00:36:54,921 --> 00:36:56,172
but please don't have him arrested.

670
00:36:57,340 --> 00:36:59,425
Arrested? I didn't have him arrested.

671
00:37:00,051 --> 00:37:01,677
But the cops came by to arrest him.

672
00:37:03,846 --> 00:37:05,181
I had nothing to do with it.

673
00:37:06,390 --> 00:37:09,560
If it wasn't you, who had him arrested?

674
00:37:12,396 --> 00:37:13,439
Let's find out.

675
00:37:13,522 --> 00:37:15,191
-Nanny Carlotta?
-[nanny] Yes, dear?

676
00:37:15,274 --> 00:37:18,319
-Please get my bag.
-[nanny] Your bag? Coming right up.

677
00:37:19,862 --> 00:37:20,905
Here you go.

678
00:37:20,988 --> 00:37:22,907
Diego and I are going to the precinct.

679
00:37:22,990 --> 00:37:24,325
-Okay, dear.
-I'll ride with you.

680
00:37:24,408 --> 00:37:25,576
Let's go.

681
00:37:27,078 --> 00:37:31,749
[unsettling music playing]

682
00:37:34,835 --> 00:37:36,504
The Mayor had him arrested.

683
00:37:37,255 --> 00:37:38,714
Of course, he did.

684
00:37:40,174 --> 00:37:44,637
He really cares about
his constituents of this town.

685
00:37:46,597 --> 00:37:49,308
Sir, I was the one who got hurt,

686
00:37:49,392 --> 00:37:52,603
and I don't plan on pressing charges
against Mr. Dolfo,

687
00:37:52,687 --> 00:37:55,481
so, please, release him now.

688
00:37:56,274 --> 00:37:57,108
Okay, ma'am.

689
00:37:57,191 --> 00:38:00,945
Since you won't press charges,
we can't keep him in here.

690
00:38:01,946 --> 00:38:04,365
Release Rodolfo Makabisbis.

691
00:38:04,448 --> 00:38:06,158
-Let him out.
-[officer] Rodolfo.

692
00:38:11,622 --> 00:38:14,208
It's Mr. Dolfo. Sir, thank you very much.

693
00:38:14,292 --> 00:38:16,085
-Diego.
-You're welcome, Ms. Aguas.

694
00:38:16,168 --> 00:38:17,628
Thank you, Officer.

695
00:38:18,296 --> 00:38:19,672
Thank you, Diego.

696
00:38:20,298 --> 00:38:22,425
Thank you, Miss Ivy.

697
00:38:23,592 --> 00:38:25,636
Please forgive me for what I did.

698
00:38:27,138 --> 00:38:28,306
[sniffling]

699
00:38:28,389 --> 00:38:29,640
It's all right, Mr. Dolfo.

700
00:38:31,684 --> 00:38:33,519
I understand why you did that.

701
00:38:34,979 --> 00:38:38,357
I know how it feels.

702
00:38:38,441 --> 00:38:40,943
[melancholic music playing]

703
00:38:41,777 --> 00:38:42,987
I know the pain…

704
00:38:44,447 --> 00:38:48,534
of losing a loved one.

705
00:38:49,201 --> 00:38:50,953
I understand how you feel.

706
00:38:53,456 --> 00:38:55,916
You're such a good person, Miss Ivy.

707
00:38:58,002 --> 00:39:00,921
Thank you so much, ma'am.

708
00:39:01,005 --> 00:39:02,423
Thank you, Diego.

709
00:39:10,973 --> 00:39:15,686
[melancholic music playing]

710
00:39:21,108 --> 00:39:25,404
Ivy, thanks again for helping
Mr. Dolfo get out of jail.

711
00:39:26,739 --> 00:39:27,865
It's nothing.

712
00:39:29,950 --> 00:39:32,203
What you said earlier…

713
00:39:33,329 --> 00:39:37,041
about knowing how it feels
to lose a loved one…

714
00:39:40,586 --> 00:39:42,588
I don't want to talk about it, Diego.

715
00:39:45,633 --> 00:39:47,968
I know you're still mad at me.

716
00:39:50,471 --> 00:39:53,265
I'm sorry. I know what I did was wrong.

717
00:39:55,684 --> 00:39:57,895
But I hope you'll forgive me.

718
00:39:59,271 --> 00:40:00,523
Diego.

719
00:40:01,107 --> 00:40:02,358
You've already apologized so many times.

720
00:40:04,735 --> 00:40:06,779
Yes, I forgive you.

721
00:40:07,655 --> 00:40:11,659
So, please, let's not talk
about this anymore.

722
00:40:13,869 --> 00:40:15,079
Okay.

723
00:40:15,746 --> 00:40:17,164
Thank you.

724
00:40:18,457 --> 00:40:20,334
Just forget about what happened.

725
00:40:21,168 --> 00:40:25,464
[melancholic music playing]

726
00:40:29,718 --> 00:40:31,178
[engine starts]

727
00:40:37,977 --> 00:40:42,356
I really hate it when someone
tries to take what's mine.

728
00:40:42,440 --> 00:40:45,651
[unsettling music playing]

729
00:40:48,112 --> 00:40:49,780
And I hate being betrayed.

730
00:40:51,157 --> 00:40:52,783
People who go behind my back.

731
00:40:59,373 --> 00:41:00,833
I need to talk to you.

732
00:41:06,088 --> 00:41:07,214
About what?

733
00:41:08,507 --> 00:41:13,220
About how you used Miss Aguas
to get Dolfo out of prison?

734
00:41:13,304 --> 00:41:17,183
Or maybe, about what her lips taste like?

735
00:41:20,186 --> 00:41:21,228
I saw you two.

736
00:41:22,146 --> 00:41:24,273
Do you think I liked what you did?

737
00:41:25,274 --> 00:41:28,194
I don't need your permission
to kiss any woman I want.

738
00:41:28,277 --> 00:41:29,904
Well, you can kiss anyone you want…

739
00:41:30,821 --> 00:41:33,407
except Miss Aguas

740
00:41:33,491 --> 00:41:35,910
because she's mine.

741
00:41:35,993 --> 00:41:37,244
[scoffs]

742
00:41:37,328 --> 00:41:38,871
Wow, Arnaldo.

743
00:41:38,954 --> 00:41:41,373
You still haven't changed.
You're like a kid.

744
00:41:41,999 --> 00:41:44,585
You still think you own whoever you like.

745
00:41:46,086 --> 00:41:47,463
Hmm.

746
00:41:47,546 --> 00:41:51,759
[tense music playing]

747
00:41:59,725 --> 00:42:02,102
So, who's the scared kid now?

748
00:42:08,025 --> 00:42:09,360
Go ahead.

749
00:42:10,528 --> 00:42:11,737
Shoot me!

750
00:42:11,820 --> 00:42:13,155
Pull the trigger!

751
00:42:17,201 --> 00:42:18,536
[rifle cocks]

752
00:42:19,954 --> 00:42:22,915
[tense music intensifies]

753
00:42:23,582 --> 00:42:24,708
Mayor.

754
00:42:26,418 --> 00:42:27,878
[tense music fades]

755
00:42:30,965 --> 00:42:31,882
Arnaldo, Diego.

756
00:42:33,133 --> 00:42:34,718
Arnaldo, cut that out.

757
00:42:35,803 --> 00:42:37,221
What's wrong with you two?

758
00:42:40,641 --> 00:42:41,475
[Arnaldo sighs]

759
00:42:42,643 --> 00:42:44,728
My brother's so brave!

760
00:42:47,690 --> 00:42:50,818
But let me just remind you
that Ivy is mine.

761
00:42:50,901 --> 00:42:54,572
And if I see you
hovering around her again…

762
00:42:57,449 --> 00:42:58,701
[clicks tongue]

763
00:43:00,578 --> 00:43:04,665
[unsettling music playing]

764
00:43:15,134 --> 00:43:19,054
That's Diego, Auntie,
picking a fight with Arnaldo again.

765
00:43:19,805 --> 00:43:21,599
You'd think after he leaves this house,

766
00:43:21,682 --> 00:43:23,851
he'd disappear for good.

767
00:43:24,393 --> 00:43:26,186
[chuckles] But I don't
want to think about him.

768
00:43:26,770 --> 00:43:29,565
It sounds like Diego's a pain in the neck.

769
00:43:29,648 --> 00:43:32,568
His very existence is a pain.

770
00:43:34,528 --> 00:43:37,281
I really admire the sacrifices
you've made, Emilia.

771
00:43:38,824 --> 00:43:42,369
You really love this family,
especially Raul.

772
00:43:43,078 --> 00:43:46,665
I'm so glad you see that.

773
00:43:48,417 --> 00:43:50,210
Meanwhile, my father…

774
00:43:51,670 --> 00:43:53,047
and other people,

775
00:43:53,631 --> 00:43:57,217
they all think I'm a fool.

776
00:43:59,094 --> 00:44:01,305
But I really don't care what they think.

777
00:44:02,348 --> 00:44:04,099
I love Raul.

778
00:44:04,183 --> 00:44:05,517
I love my family.

779
00:44:06,143 --> 00:44:07,770
I love being an Ardiente.

780
00:44:10,022 --> 00:44:11,690
I have to hold this together,

781
00:44:11,774 --> 00:44:13,233
no matter what happens.

782
00:44:13,942 --> 00:44:16,779
[unsettling music playing]

783
00:44:17,863 --> 00:44:19,531
And how is your father doing?

784
00:44:21,742 --> 00:44:23,661
I don't know. I don't want to know.

785
00:44:24,536 --> 00:44:25,496
And why not?

786
00:44:25,579 --> 00:44:29,792
Aren't you excited for him
to return alive and limping?

787
00:44:29,875 --> 00:44:31,126
Not now.

788
00:44:31,210 --> 00:44:32,795
I'm just getting started.

789
00:44:34,713 --> 00:44:38,050
You're only just starting to fail, Emilia.

790
00:44:39,009 --> 00:44:41,929
I'm updated on everything
that's happening here.

791
00:44:42,012 --> 00:44:45,307
And all I can say is
you still have a long way to go

792
00:44:45,391 --> 00:44:47,351
to be at par with your father.

793
00:44:49,853 --> 00:44:52,272
I can surpass all he's done.

794
00:44:52,981 --> 00:44:54,608
I just need to be more careful.

795
00:44:55,234 --> 00:44:56,693
I can't afford to make any more mistakes.

796
00:44:57,444 --> 00:44:58,862
I'm here to help you.

797
00:45:01,323 --> 00:45:02,616
That's why I'm back.

798
00:45:08,080 --> 00:45:09,790
For your success, dear.

799
00:45:25,764 --> 00:45:27,307
I'm just here to get my other things.

800
00:45:27,391 --> 00:45:28,475
[door clicks shut]

801
00:45:32,980 --> 00:45:37,234
I guess you're really going
to leave this house, huh?

802
00:45:39,778 --> 00:45:40,737
Son.

803
00:45:41,697 --> 00:45:42,739
Diego.

804
00:45:43,240 --> 00:45:45,534
Whatever happened between you and Arnaldo,

805
00:45:46,326 --> 00:45:47,703
I hope you can let it go.

806
00:45:48,912 --> 00:45:50,539
Dad.

807
00:45:50,622 --> 00:45:52,583
I'm so sick and tired
of understanding him.

808
00:45:53,750 --> 00:45:56,962
-She's just a woman, son.
-This isn't just about Ivy.

809
00:45:57,045 --> 00:45:59,339
This is about everything he's done to me.

810
00:46:01,341 --> 00:46:04,720
Son, you know your brother.
You know what he can do.

811
00:46:04,803 --> 00:46:07,306
-I'm not scared of him.
-Well, I'm scared for you.

812
00:46:08,390 --> 00:46:11,310
So, keep out of his way
as much as you can.

813
00:46:11,393 --> 00:46:14,188
What for, Dad? So he can bother Ivy again?

814
00:46:14,271 --> 00:46:16,440
He already has Natalie.
Why does he even need Ivy?

815
00:46:16,523 --> 00:46:17,608
Why? Do you like Ivy?

816
00:46:17,691 --> 00:46:20,819
[tender music playing]

817
00:46:30,204 --> 00:46:33,582
[sighs] I can't explain
how I feel about her.

818
00:46:36,001 --> 00:46:39,004
But it feels like I've known her
for a long time.

819
00:46:41,715 --> 00:46:43,509
I want to get to know her more.

820
00:46:43,592 --> 00:46:45,969
I want to protect her from Arnaldo.

821
00:46:47,429 --> 00:46:52,559
[tender music intensifies]

822
00:47:03,737 --> 00:47:05,239
<i>Butchoy has a love letter for you.</i>

823
00:47:05,322 --> 00:47:06,782
<i>Butchoy is so cute.</i>

824
00:47:06,865 --> 00:47:09,326
<i>I guess I've got more competition now.</i>

825
00:47:09,409 --> 00:47:11,036
<i>Are we celebrating something?</i>

826
00:47:11,119 --> 00:47:12,746
<i>It's final. I'm running for Senate.</i>

827
00:47:13,413 --> 00:47:15,499
[Pablo] <i>I have</i>
<i>a different candidate in mind.</i>

828
00:47:15,582 --> 00:47:16,667
<i>A different candidate?</i>

829
00:47:16,750 --> 00:47:17,709
<i>I like the sound of that.</i>

830
00:47:17,793 --> 00:47:21,547
<i>Miss Aguas, I was born to lead.</i>
<i>And this is my chance.</i>

831
00:47:21,630 --> 00:47:25,300
<i>I'd rather support Emilia than you.</i>

832
00:47:25,384 --> 00:47:27,219
<i>What can I do to change your mind?</i>

833
00:47:27,302 --> 00:47:28,845
<i>The farmers' land.</i>

834
00:47:28,929 --> 00:47:31,598
<i>Are you doing this</i>
<i>for the farmers or for Diego?</i>

835
00:47:31,682 --> 00:47:36,436
[Ivy] <i>It's not my fault if your brother</i>
<i>moves faster than you.</i>

836
00:47:36,520 --> 00:47:39,481
[theme music playing]
